OpenGong is made of three kinds of work, each under its own license. All three
let you use, modify, share and sell the work, as long as you credit the
original author and keep the license notice.

  Hardware designs   hardware/, Placement Jig/, Sensor Cover/, Box Bracket/
                     CERN Open Hardware Licence v2 - Permissive (CERN-OHL-P-2.0)
                     Full text: LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt

  Firmware and app   firmware/
                     MIT License (MIT)
                     Full text: firmware/LICENSE

  Documentation      docs/, README.md and all other files
  and images         Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
                     Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt

How to give credit
------------------
If you use, build or adapt OpenGong, credit it like this (or similar), in
your documentation, product page or about screen:

    Based on OpenGong by somekid6 (some_kid6) - https://github.com/somekid6/OpenGong

and note whether you changed it.

Exceptions
----------
The papers in docs/Reference Materials/ are the work of their authors
(M. Waterman and D. Salazar) and are not covered by these licenses.
